title: 'Jeff''s own definition: "dreaming = memory consolidation, checking*, hypothesis formation, testing, pruning", the * being "checking against the transcript".'
pid: d6b86b48-5d7f-411c-a0af-4e6b3215135c
body: |2-
  [[id:02622a8d-c00d-4f6d-bc60-d581dbe00bef][long-term memory and dreaming]], in his "using AI". Read.
  Two of his five our practices do not do: checking a note against the
  transcript it came from, and testing a hypothesis. His other note,
  [[id:62525c14-fca3-48f9-9599-fb5484e14651][? incorporate dreaming]], means something else: undirected thought, art
  and fiction, kept in a separate folder. Nothing I read measures that.
